       resources by scanning ahead of the parser specifically to start
       fetches early, independent of script timing — so this cannot
       fully prevent an eager fetch that the scanner already queued
       before this script runs, for any image already ahead in the
       markup. It is still strictly earlier and therefore strictly
       better than applying the same attributes at the end of body
       (Banynova.perf.applyLazyLoadingToPostImages, kept below as a
       fallback for any images inserted dynamically after this point).
